  "ready": true,
  "readyNote": "re-measured 11/10/2026 with the per-element probe (heading and text kinds added) on the published quickstart/ja-social-ii/j6 1.0.2 (webroot sha256 dd6a3190…; tasks/evidence/ds-remeasure-4-2026-10-11/ja-social-ii-j6): first 4/12 — the accent-text, muted and body kinds sampled nothing (no #t3-mainbody or .t3-sl on the home page), the kept dark bands' 33 elements took the worn page's text colour, the testimonial quote and author (#333333, #666666 by rules of their own) read 1.27-3.53:1 on a dark page, and the phone logo's white name read 1.94:1 on MotherDuck's accent. The kinds now read the whole wrapper, the dark bands' #44494c is given back, the logo cell is kept, the testimonial takes the system's text and muted colours; the carousel indicators' labels (pushed out of their 14 px dots) are no longer read as text (flow.mjs). Then 12/12 with Moxie, MotherDuck, Toggl Track and Apple, controls 0, kept bands 0 differences, no text under 4.5:1 worse than the template's own (the lowest, 1.78, is the template's own), 54% or more of the page follows, every contrast kind sampled in every view, dark and light screenshots looked at. Earlier: measured 10/10/2026 on ja-social-ii/j6 1.0.2 (tasks/evidence/followups-2026-10-10/p6-dsdata/ready-templates.txt): 12/12, default unchanged, no text made less readable than the template's own under the systems tried, 55% or more of the page follows; its body probe now reads the running text, not the slider caption, and its container probe the page container, not a half-width slide column",
  "contrastNote": "re-measured 11/10/2026: the home page has no #t3-mainbody and no .t3-sl, so the first three kinds sampled nothing (the probe must find at least one element); they now read the whole wrapper: its links (accent-text), its paragraphs (muted, body) and list items (body); heading and text judge every visible heading and text element",
